# The E5's 9-key keypad has neither Enter nor BackSpace: its confirm key (matrix
# row 1, column 0) emits KEY_SELECT and its back key (row 0, column 0) emits
# KEY_BACK -- neither of which anything in the session handles.  phosh's lock screen
# submits on KP_Enter, and a locked screen with digits in it can then only be cleared
# with the on-screen keypad, so the back key becomes BackSpace.
#
# The scancode is the *matrix scan code* (MATRIX_SCAN_CODE(row, col, row_shift) with
# 4 rows x 7 columns, so row_shift 3), not the keycode the key produces: evdev's
# EVIOCSKEYCODE indexes dev->keycode[], whose size is rows*cols = 28, and using the
# keycode (353) as the index is what makes such a call fail with EINVAL -- the
# mistake that once made this look like "the keypad cannot be remapped at all".
# tools/keycode-query.py reads and writes exactly this map.
#
# /etc lives in the initramfs overlay and is rewritten on every boot;
# systemd-hwdb-update.service (WantedBy=sysinit.target) recompiles
# /etc/udev/hwdb.bin when this file is newer, and udev's keyboard builtin applies
# the mapping when the keypad device appears.
evdev:input:b0000v0000p0000e0000*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_8=kpenter
 KEYBOARD_KEY_0=backspace
